# This repo is scoped to just the custom child theme + project docs -
# see CLAUDE.md's "What is NOT in this folder". WordPress core, plugins,
# other themes, and the database are deliberately not tracked here: core/
# plugins are managed by the host and add nothing but update-noise diffs,
# and the database (all page content, Elementor's header/footer, the
# homepage's template assignment) isn't file-based to begin with - moving
# the site means a real DB export/import, not a git pull.
#
# Ignore everything by default, then explicitly un-ignore the paths that
# are actually hand-written source for this project.
/*
!/wp-content/
/wp-content/*
!/wp-content/themes/
/wp-content/themes/*
!/wp-content/themes/oceanwp-child/
!/design-system/
!/CLAUDE.md
!/.gitignore
!/.cpanel.yml

# Even inside the tracked theme folder, don't track secrets, DB dumps, or
# OS/editor cruft that might land in there.
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.sql.zip
*.log
error_log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
node_modules/
vendor/
# ...except the theme's own checked-in copy of Google's model-viewer: the live
# site is deployed from git, so the script has to be in the repo.
!wp-content/themes/oceanwp-child/assets/js/vendor/
package-lock.json
